WEBVTT

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:10.660
<v Grace Liu>Morning, everyone. Monday the first of June. Everyone on? I won't ask how you feel about the football last night.</v>

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.989
<v Callum Reid>Probably safer not to. Better subject: the charity bake sale on Friday. Those brownies were decent.</v>

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:25.559
<v Aisha Begum>The charity bake sale on Friday has ruined shop-bought cake for me. Although yours needed a bandsaw, Callum.</v>

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.410
<v Fiona Doyle>Structural flapjack. There's a market for that.</v>

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.560
<v Grace Liu>Right, before this becomes a materials review. Finished bits first, then what we're actually taking on.</v>

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:44.049
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, tested the fire panel yesterday and it's all fine now. That's closed, nothing new off that.</v>

00:00:45.259 --> 00:00:48.060
<v Hannah Price>Lovely. Nice to have one that's actually finished.</v>

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:56.229
<v Aisha Begum>And I tested the line 2 yesterday and it's all fine now. Same thing, done rather than something for today's list.</v>

00:00:57.799 --> 00:00:59.899
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, understood. Not carrying that over.</v>

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:09.000
<v Grace Liu>I noticed the turbine one was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Just an observation, not raising another job.</v>

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.000
<v Tomasz Nowak>It settled while they were still running, yeah?</v>

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.879
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, it came back down. Nothing further coming out of that here.</v>

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:26.349
<v Grace Liu>Other bit: the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the cooling tower. That's still blocked, not a fresh action this morning.</v>

00:01:27.609 --> 00:01:31.459
<v Fiona Doyle>Right. No confirmed delivery to build anything round, then. Still blocked.</v>

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:38.590
<v Callum Reid>And we can't get to the GT2 until production gives us a window. We haven't got that window.</v>

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.370
<v Grace Liu>Understood. GT2 stays blocked; we're not pretending we've agreed access.</v>

00:01:45.849 --> 00:01:50.400
<v Grace Liu>Fiona Doyle, can you take vibration readings on the GT1 tomorrow? Normal priority.</v>

00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:56.430
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, no, I can't take that one on. I haven't got the capacity for the readings.</v>

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.799
<v Callum Reid>Grace, could you take that instead? The GT1 readings, same timing.</v>

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:09.500
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll take vibration readings on the GT1 tomorrow. Normal priority. That's with me instead of Fiona Doyle.</v>

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:14.210
<v Fiona Doyle>Thanks. Grace on that one, tomorrow, normal priority. Got it.</v>

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:21.159
<v Grace Liu>Then there's the pressure drop on the Water Booster Pump. That needs investigating.</v>

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:26.449
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll investigate the pressure drop on the Water Booster Pump. It's urgent, that one.</v>

00:02:28.259 --> 00:02:31.409
<v Aisha Begum>Is that being lumped in with the filter, or—</v>

00:02:33.169 --> 00:02:38.419
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, sorry, separate. I'm investigating the pressure drop, not assuming the filter is the cause.</v>

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:45.080
<v Grace Liu>Okay, Tomasz Nowak has the Water Booster Pump pressure-drop investigation, and it's urgent.</v>

00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:54.919
<v Grace Liu>On the filter itself, I'll swap the filter on the water booster today. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:02:55.759 --> 00:03:00.659
<v Callum Reid>So that one's definitely today, just not the same urgency as the pressure drop?</v>

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.650
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. Today, but not an emergency.</v>

00:03:05.939 --> 00:03:11.189
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, Grace Liu for the water booster filter. Two separate jobs, not one duplicated line.</v>

00:03:12.169 --> 00:03:18.469
<v Grace Liu>Olumide Adeyemi, can you recalibrate the sensors on the line 1 mould temp on the 3rd? Fairly important.</v>

00:03:18.919 --> 00:03:23.120
<v Olumide Adeyemi>On the 3rd, so Wednesday, yeah? Not pulling that into this morning?</v>

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:28.530
<v Grace Liu>Yes, on the 3rd. Fairly important, but that is the agreed timing.</v>

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:34.099
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, accepted. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the line 1 mould temp on the 3rd.</v>

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:40.250
<v Hannah Price>And that's a recalibration, rather than just checking what the display says?</v>

00:03:42.379 --> 00:03:45.180
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, recalibrate the sensors. That's what I'm taking.</v>

00:03:45.819 --> 00:03:55.270
<v Grace Liu>Hannah, can you go to Northfield Substation to pick up the replacement parts for the Forklift Fleet tomorrow? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:56.129 --> 00:04:01.379
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, just to be clear, that's the collection we're agreeing, not fitting them as well?</v>

00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:09.550
<v Grace Liu>Just collection. Northfield Substation, replacement parts for the Forklift Fleet. Tomorrow, first because it's holding production up.</v>

00:04:10.189 --> 00:04:17.540
<v Hannah Price>Okay, I'll go to Northfield Substation to pick up the replacement parts for the Forklift Fleet tomorrow. I'll do that first.</v>

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.769
<v Fiona Doyle>Collection only against Hannah, then. No fitting job implied.</v>

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:28.199
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, the production hold is why that one's right up there.</v>

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:37.000
<v Hannah Price>And I'll check the guarding on the IM1 after lunch. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:04:38.759 --> 00:04:44.709
<v Grace Liu>Thanks, Hannah Price. IM1 guarding check after lunch, first in that slot because it's holding production up.</v>

00:04:46.259 --> 00:04:49.759
<v Hannah Price>Yep, that's what I mean. After lunch, that comes first.</v>

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:56.089
<v Callum Reid>Right. And a check on the list isn't the same as saying it's already okay to run.</v>

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:02.750
<v Grace Liu>Absolutely. We've agreed the guarding check, not a result before it's happened.</v>

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:10.300
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll inspect the Boiler Feedwater Pump for leaks tomorrow as well. Normal priority for that.</v>

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.720
<v Fiona Doyle>Tomasz for the Boiler Feedwater Pump leak inspection, tomorrow, normal priority?</v>

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:18.500
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's right. Separate from the urgent pressure-drop investigation.</v>

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:25.480
<v Aisha Begum>I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Boiler Feedwater Pump by 11am. That's fairly important.</v>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:33.399
<v Grace Liu>Thanks, Aisha. Permit to work and isolation for the Boiler Feedwater Pump by 11am, fairly important.</v>

00:05:34.129 --> 00:05:38.329
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, both parts of that are mine. Not just the permit paperwork.</v>

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.939
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. That doesn't change my leak inspection from tomorrow.</v>

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.180
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. Different timing for the two. The permit and isolation—</v>

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:55.350
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talking over you. You went all robot for a second.</v>

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.389
<v Grace Liu>We lost half that sentence here too. Go again?</v>

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:10.660
<v Fiona Doyle>Just the timings: Aisha's permit and isolation by 11am, Grace Liu's water booster filter today. The Boiler Feedwater Pump leak inspection is tomorrow.</v>

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:19.360
<v Hannah Price>And my two aren't competing in the same slot: IM1 guarding after lunch, Forklift Fleet parts from Northfield Substation tomorrow.</v>

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:28.860
<v Callum Reid>Both production holds, so first after lunch for the guarding, first tomorrow for the collection. That's how I've heard it.</v>

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.740
<v Hannah Price>Yep, exactly.</v>

00:06:33.629 --> 00:06:40.980
<v Grace Liu>Good. And just so the blocked bits don't creep into the agreed work: still no supplier confirmation for the cooling tower.</v>

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:46.790
<v Callum Reid>Same with GT2. No production window, still blocked. Nothing taken on against it.</v>

00:06:48.899 --> 00:06:53.449
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the fire panel stays in the finished column. Yesterday's test was fine.</v>

00:06:55.689 --> 00:06:59.189
<v Aisha Begum>Same for line 2. Finished yesterday, not another job today.</v>

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:04.519
<v Grace Liu>Right, that's the agreed list. Thanks, everyone. Teams has mostly behaved for once.</v>

00:07:06.589 --> 00:07:07.990
<v Callum Reid>Unlike the flapjack, apparently.</v>

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.810
<v Grace Liu>It had excellent load-bearing properties. Cheers, all.</v>
